Currently, passing MessageElementType=EnumValue will always crash.
We're constructing a `metadata` object in `ClusterDataCopier::AnyBuilderAddValue` that has no `_owner`, but then we pass that to `ClusterDataCopier::CopyEnumFromCluster`, which immediately tries to dereference metadata->_owner:

```cpp
    bool ClusterDataCopier::AnyBuilderAddValue(LVMessage& message, LVMessageMetadataType valueType, bool isRepeated, int protobufIndex, int8_t* value)
    {
        auto metadata = std::make_shared<MessageElementMetadata>(valueType, isRepeated, protobufIndex);
        switch (valueType)
        {
        // ...
        case LVMessageMetadataType::EnumValue:
            CopyEnumFromCluster(metadata, value, message);
            break;

// ...

    void ClusterDataCopier::CopyEnumFromCluster(const std::shared_ptr<const MessageElementMetadata> metadata, int8_t* start, LVMessage& message)
    {
        std::shared_ptr<EnumMetadata> enumMetadata = metadata->_owner->FindEnumMetadata(metadata->embeddedMessageName);
```   

So, first is a minor fix: throw `InvalidEnumValueException` instead of dereferencing null, which translates to a nice `-2003` error code in LabVIEW.

But the bigger fix is to better support that enum data type w/ the Any builder part of the API. I did that by adding a new exported function called `AnyBuilderAddValueFromMetadata` that takes in a metadata owner (i.e. the grpc client) and looks up the enum metadata from there.

Here's what it looks like on the LV side:
![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2b0081c9-729d-4a54-b5ef-9e1a5e74d65d)

And I also added a test to the "deprecated" section side by side with the existing **SimpleAnyBuilder.vi** test.
This one tests the interoperability with the existing `AnyBuilderAddValue` and also tests the error case with an invalid enum value:

![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1a5373a0-c78a-4122-a5f4-59ece65d5131)

This test required making `Element to Enum Metadata.vi` public

